<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kukawa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kukawa is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borno-state">Borno State</a> in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, near the western shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-chad">Lake Chad</a>. It was founded in 1814 by the scholar and war leader Muhammad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-amin">al-Amin</a> al-Kanemi and became the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bornu">Bornu</a> under his family. A busy market on the trans-Saharan routes, it was visited by European travellers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-barth">Heinrich Barth</a>. In 1893 the warlord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rabih-az-zubayr">Rabih az-Zubayr</a> captured and destroyed it.</p></div>
